    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/06/saucony-triumph-23-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The full-length PWRRUN PB midsole is soft and highly cushioned with good impact protection for daily/long runs; heel feel is plush with a beveled rearfoot that can feel slightly clunky early, while the forefoot is mildly flexible and finishes slightly snappy.",
        "Responsiveness: Versus Triumph 22, ride feel is clearly bouncier and more responsive, and the lighter weight improves turnover; it supports easy-to-mild uptempo efforts but is not a top-end speed shoe.",
        "Stability: This is a neutral shoe with mild guidance from a wider/stiffer platform (including mild torsional control), deep sidewalls, medial heel flare, and a stiff padded heel counter; upper lockdown and lateral hold are good for running but rearfoot bias may not suit runners needing strong lateral stability.",
        "Durability: Durability is lower than prior Triumph versions, with early outsole wear seen around 30 miles on exposed PWRRUN PB and risk of posterolateral XT-900 rubber peeling; expected longevity is average overall."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/05/saucony-triumph-23-review-soft-and-fun.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The softer PWRRUN PB blend gives a plush heel and forefoot feel with strong impact protection, and the 37/27 mm stack plus broad heel helps disperse landings without feeling mushy.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is energetic with noticeable bounce and rebound, but forefoot toe-off is less snappy at faster paces and would benefit from a firmer front.",
        "Stability: A broad platform, 10 mm drop, rigid supportive heel counter, and secure upper create solid stability; reduced midfoot rubber and a narrower midfoot make it slightly less stable but more flexible.",
        "Durability: The outsole has strategic rubber with less midfoot coverage and new forefoot mini-lugs, with good grip reported so far; the dense thick upper suggests good material longevity, though long-term wear is not fully detailed."
      ]
    }
